I haven't been doing YAAPs for a while now, but I thought I'd do one
for this 17.5k-turn ascension with a randomly-chosen character, which
I know is hardly record-breaking but it's my best by over 10k.

As happens with some regularity on NAO, I got helpful bones. I got
SDSM, CoMR, and two magic markers in a double-bones Minetown, and it
wasn't long after that when I decided to try for a fast ascension. I
dug down for a few levels after finding Sokoban (which I only did one
level of), then after finding the quest portal just outright did a
levelport to level 30, which in an odd coincidence happened to be the
VotD. Where a vampire lord proceeded to take two levels off me before
I remembered to put my cloak back on. :-) (I know, I'm sure I didn't
need to take it off in the first place, but levelporting isn't
something I normally do so I was being "careful".) I did the castle
and got to the wand at just under 8k turns, finally getting speed
boots. Getting into the quest was fiddly as despite clearing out the
castle and VotD I was still only level 13, but a bit of polypiling
soon got me a gain-level potion.

I used magic mapping scrolls and digging to get through most of
Gehennom quickly. Orcus summoned Demogorgon which was a bit of a
scare, but I'd kept a non-wrest wish spare so a rubber chicken soon
sorted them out. I got the Amulet at about 12k turns.

On the way up I ran into Asmodeus, having originally dug down on his
level without realising, and later on had a run-in with an Archon in a
treasure zoo (which I didn't handle terribly well). Mapping the levels
I'd skipped with the Amulet wasn't as fast as I'd hoped, frankly, but
it did the job.

The planes were awkward mainly due to not having the spell-based
confusion I'm used to, and being rather lacking in items I only had
one potion of booze. So I relied on stumbling into the portals on
Earth and to some extent Air. The monsters soon found it for me on
Fire, and on Water I finally used the potion - not that it did me much
good, the portal got covered up by an item as usual. Astral actually
wasn't too bad given my iffy HP and AC (I ended up not needing
conflict at all), and the first altar was the right one.

